From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sun4i: vi_scaler: Scale the chroma phase by the subsampling

The chroma phase registers count chroma samples: YUV 4:2:0 already
programs half the luma phase (and the -0.25 vertical siting). YUV 4:2:2
and 4:1:1 got the luma phase unchanged, which shifts chroma by hsub - 1
luma pixels for each pixel the crop starts off the chroma grid. Divide
by the subsampling factors for every format.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_vi_scaler.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_vi_scaler.c
@@ -972,13 +972,12 @@
 		vphase = 0;
 		chphase = 0xfffe0000;
 		cvphase = 0xfffe0000;
-	} else if (format->hsub == 2 && format->vsub == 2) {
-		chphase = hphase >> 1;
-		cvphase = (vphase >> 1) -
-			(1UL << (SUN8I_VI_SCALER_SCALE_FRAC - 2));
 	} else {
-		chphase = hphase;
-		cvphase = vphase;
+		/* chroma phases count chroma samples */
+		chphase = hphase / format->hsub;
+		cvphase = vphase / format->vsub;
+		if (format->vsub == 2)
+			cvphase -= 1UL << (SUN8I_VI_SCALER_SCALE_FRAC - 2);
 	}
 
 	if (layer->cfg->de_type >= SUN8I_MIXER_DE3) {
